## How to read this file

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **ID** | Unique within this methodology. Format: `<CATEGORY>-<MODULE>-<N>` or `<PREFIX>-<N>`. See `00-methodology.md`. |
| **Type** | `bug`, `gap`, `idea`, `risk`, `opportunity`, `regression` |
| **Module** | Area of the codebase (or `[SHARED]` for cross-module) |
| **Summary** | One-line description |
| **Status** | `open` · `doing` · `done` · `dropped` (see [`00-global.md` §6](../../../skills/aidex-conventions/references/00-global.md#6-status-vocabulary)) |
| **Severity** | P0 (critical) · P1 (high) · P2 (medium) · P3 (low) |
| **First Seen** | `YYYY-MM-DD` — audit run that first recorded it |
| **Last Updated** | `YYYY-MM-DD` — most recent change to this row |
| **Audit Runs** | Comma-separated list of run folders that confirmed this finding |
| **Escalated To** | `<type>/<filename>` (D-03) — backlog entry, plan, or decision. Empty when not yet escalated. |
| **Notes** | Triage notes, reason for `dropped`, closing commit, etc. |

